<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Power Items</h1>
<p>Power items are magic items from Valhalla's early days, when players got 
them for donations. Valhalla takes no donations any more, and the 
players who have power items keep them. They include anklets, girdles, 
rings, bracelets, back plates and sashes, most of them raising one of 
your abilities, and a few with powers of their own.
</p><p>A power item is yours alone. With <a cmd='#'>Help Piset</a> you may give it a title 
and descriptions of your own, once. A power item bag holds them without 
taking up room in your inventory (see <a cmd='#'>Help Pibag</a>).
</p><p><b>The mana palm orb</b> is burnt into its owner's palm and takes up no 
place on the body. It stores mana for later:
</p>
<pre>examine orb              how much it holds
touch hand to head       store mana in it
touch hand to heart      take the mana back
</pre>
<p>It doesn't work while you are fighting, nor for 5 minutes after a fight 
with another player.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Piset</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Pibag</a>
</pre>




</div>